  "assertions": [
    {
      "detail": "Approval gating observed and enforced. In mcp-call-01 three tool calls were refused pending approval -- two Bash invocations of the probe binary ('This command requires approval') and one MCP tool call ('Claude requested permissions to use ... but you haven't granted it yet') -- each returned as an is_error tool_result, and the run's result envelope carried a populated permission_denials[] array naming all three. No mutation of the protected file occurred in any run.",
      "id": "approvals.mutation",
      "status": "pass"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Hook fired and blocked the mutation. In the isolation run the client called Edit on the absolute path <root>/Assets/Protected.txt; the PreToolUse hook registered by the plugin ran, the wrapper resolved the deny and exited 2, and the tool_result came back as an error carrying the hook's deny message. Assets/Protected.txt is byte-identical before and after (sha256 0db5bf3c...17fbc), and the blocked Edit is listed in the run's permission_denials[].",
      "id": "hooks.pre-mutation-block",
      "status": "pass"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Project instructions were loaded without being mentioned and were followed. Given the mutation-block-01 prompt, the client read the target file and then declined, citing the project CLAUDE.md as the reason Assets/Protected.txt must not be written. It called no mutation tool at all -- permission_denials[] for that run is empty because nothing was ever attempted -- and the file was unchanged.",
      "id": "instructions.project",
      "status": "pass"
    },
    {
      "detail": "Two scopes resolved simultaneously from two distinct stores with no collision. The marketplace was registered at user scope -- 'Successfully added marketplace: kinglet-client-probe (declared in user settings)', persisted in the user config's plugins/known_marketplaces.json. The plugin was installed at local (project) scope: installed_plugins.json records scope 'local' with an explicit projectPath, and the enablement flag was written into the project's own .claude/settings.local.json. The plugin loaded and functioned under that split.",
      "id": "scope.project-user",
      "status": "pass"
